{
    "background_story": "Kelly was a Scottish expat living in the United States, and she took great pride in her heritage. Every year, she would participate in the local Highland games, where she would showcase her skills in traditional Scottish sports. But Kelly's true passion was baking, and she was particularly famous for her delicious jambos - a traditional Scottish sweet biscuit. She spent years perfecting her recipe, experimenting with different ingredients and techniques. Eventually, Kelly's jambos gained a loyal following, and she started selling them at local farmers' markets. As her business grew, Kelly became known as the 'Jambos Queen,' and her tasty treats brought a taste of Scotland to the American community.",
